@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bmfire-nouns`
IMPORT `bmfire-insuring-clause`
IMPORT `bmfire-perils`
IMPORT `bmfire-exclusions`
IMPORT `bmfire-indemnity`
IMPORT `bmfire-conditions`
IMPORT `bmfire-claim`
IMPORT `bmfire-fixtures`

-- EVIDENCE FOR THE FINDINGS (NOTES.md, "Findings"). Each assertion states what the Rules,
-- read as written, give in a scenario a policyholder's or the insurer's lawyer would
-- raise. These assertions PASS: they demonstrate a surprising answer of the text, they do
-- not test a correct one. The finding numbers are NOTES.md's.

§ `Findings`

§§ `X1 — risk J covers the Insured's own vehicles and animals`

-- J has no exclusion; its only sentence on the Insured's own vehicles is about the
-- deductible. The Insured's own lorry hitting the building is covered, less the deductible.
`the Insured's own lorry` MEANS
    `a building claim in` (`a 2026 Summary` `every risk` 1500000000 (LIST (`a deductible for` `risk J` `of` 10000000))) `risk J`
        (LIST `fact — impact by a vehicle`, `fact — the vehicle or animal was owned or controlled by the Insured, the occupier of the insured premises, or their employees`) EMPTY EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons` `the Insured's own lorry` EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the amount payable` `the Insured's own lorry` EQUALS 190000000

§§ `X2 — terrorism by a person acting alone, or for a government, is not excluded from B or D`

`a lone bomber` MEANS LIST `fact — an explosion`, `fact — violence or force was used or threatened`, `fact — for a political, religious, ideological or similar purpose`
#ASSERT `I — Terrorism` (`the facts` `a lone bomber`)
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk B` `a lone bomber` EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk D` (`fact — an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order` FOLLOWED BY `a lone bomber`) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `X3 — riot cover under D is taken back by III.1(a)(iii)`

-- The same riot, D insured. Called "civil commotion" (bạo động dân sự), III.1(a)(i) gives
-- it back to D; called "Nổi loạn", which (i) also names, (iii) excludes it outright.
`rioters and a commotion` MEANS LIST `fact — an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order`, `fact — a civil commotion`
`rioters and a riot` MEANS LIST `fact — an act of a person taking part with others in disturbing public order`, `fact — a riot or rebellion, the event III.1(a)(i) and III.1(a)(iii) both name`
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk D` `rioters and a commotion` EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY
#ASSERT NOT `III.1(a)(i) — riot, civil commotion, strike or lockout, risk D not insured` (`a building claim` `risk D` `rioters and a riot` EMPTY EMPTY)
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk D` `rioters and a riot` EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `III.1(a)(iii) — rebellion, mutiny, rising, insurrection, revolution, riot, coup, martial law`

§§ `X5 — average, then contribution, reduce twice`

-- Building worth 1,000; insured here for 600 and under another policy for 600 (1,200 in
-- all, more than its value). Damage 200: average gives 120, contribution halves it, 60.
-- Each insurer applying the same Rules pays 60: 120 of a 200 loss, though over-insured.
`over-insured with two policies` MEANS
    `the amount payable`
        (`a claim for the loss` `the Summary` `risk A` `fire`
            (`a loss in full` (`an item` "the warehouse building" 600000000 1000000000 EMPTY) `physical loss, destruction or damage` 200000000 EMPTY
                (`The other figures of a loss` WITH `marine recovery` IS 0, `other insurance` IS JUST (`Other insurance on the item` WITH `its sum insured for the item` IS 600000000, `it excludes or rateably limits its share alongside this policy` IS FALSE), `restoring cost` IS 0, `blank media` IS 0, `copying` IS 0)))
#ASSERT `over-insured with two policies` EQUALS 60000000

§§ `X6 — a warranty bites only in a renewal period`

`a fire, sprinkler warranty broken, first period` MEANS
    `a claim in full` (`a 2026 Summary in full` `every risk` 1500000000 EMPTY FALSE FALSE FALSE) `risk A` `the day` (`the facts` `fire`)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY
        (LIST (`A warranty` WITH `description` IS "sprinklers maintained", `not complied with during the period of insurance` IS TRUE))
        (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) (LIST `lapse — insured the deductible during the period of the policy`)) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `VI.5 — a warranty not complied with during the period` `a fire, sprinkler warranty broken, first period`
#ASSERT `the amount payable` `a fire, sprinkler warranty broken, first period` EQUALS 200000000

§§ `X7 — the twelve months to sue run while the arbitration is still being formed`

-- Bao Minh rejects the amount claimed on 15 March 2026 and the Insured asks for
-- arbitration the same day. Two months to agree one arbitrator, then two months to
-- appoint each; an umpire with no period; an award with no period. No suit by 16 March
-- 2027: the benefit is lost under (b)(i), whether or not an award has come.
#ASSERT `VII.8 — the end of two months from receipt` (`VII.8 — the end of two months from receipt` (YMD 2026 3 15)) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 15
#ASSERT `VII.2(b)(i) — the benefit of the rejected claim is lost` (YMD 2026 3 15) NOTHING (YMD 2027 3 16)

§§ `X8 — an empty building: water damage excluded at once, the policy ended at 30 days`

-- I(ii) excludes the empty building's water damage however short the time empty; VI.3(b)
-- ends the cover only after 30 days. Empty since 31 May, a pipe bursts on 1 June.
`a burst pipe in a building empty one day` MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk I` `the day` (`the facts` (LIST `fact — water overflowing from a water tank, water apparatus or water pipe`))
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` (`the building with` (LIST `item — a building left empty or not in use`)) `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY
        (LIST (`A change under condition VI.3` WITH `kind` IS `the insured building, or the building holding insured property, left empty`, `date it began` IS YMD 2026 5 31, `Bao Minh consented by an endorsement before the DAMAGE` IS FALSE))
        EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) EMPTY) FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT `VI.3 — the policy had ceased for the property lost` `a burst pipe in a building empty one day`
#ASSERT `the reasons` `a burst pipe in a building empty one day` EQUALS LIST `II.I(ii) — DAMAGE to a building left empty or not in use`

§§ `X9 — three answers to "must the premium be paid first?"`

-- Premium paid on 20 January; fire on 15 January.
`a fire before the premium is paid` MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` (YMD 2026 1 15) (`the facts` `fire`)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        (`a premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 20))) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 1 25) EMPTY) FALSE 0
-- The preamble: not covered ("sau khi đã đóng phí").
#ASSERT NOT `preamble — the premium required had been paid before the DAMAGE` (`a premium paid on` (JUST (YMD 2026 1 20))) (YMD 2026 1 15)
-- VIII.3 as encoded: covered.
#ASSERT `the amount payable` `a fire before the premium is paid` EQUALS 200000000
-- Premium never paid; fire on 15 January. Clause 1 read alone: no liability. Clause 2
-- (encoded): liable for the period in force, so covered.
`a fire, premium never paid` MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk A` (YMD 2026 1 15) (`the facts` `fire`)
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        (`a premium paid on` NOTHING) EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY (`conduct` (YMD 2026 1 25) EMPTY) FALSE 0
#ASSERT NOT `VIII.3.1 — the condition precedent, read without clause 2` `a fire, premium never paid`
#ASSERT `the amount payable` `a fire, premium never paid` EQUALS 200000000

§§ `X10 — the electrical exclusion takes out lightning damage to the machine struck`

`a lightning strike on the press` MEANS
    `a claim for the loss` `the Summary` `risk A` (LIST `fact — a direct lightning strike`, `fact — the lightning changed the shape of the property or set it alight`)
        (`physical damage to` (`an item` "printing press" 400000000 400000000 (LIST `item — electrical machinery, apparatus or installation`)) `of` 150000000
            `with` (LIST `loss — the item itself suffered over-running, excessive pressure, short-circuiting, self-heating, arcing or leakage of electricity`))
#ASSERT `the reasons` `a lightning strike on the press` EQUALS LIST `III.1(c) — electrical machinery damaged by its own electrical fault`

§§ `X11 — the date-change write-back leaves out flood and water`

-- A date fault in a pump controller lets a river flood the site: under H (flood), out;
-- the same fault and a storm under H, in.
`a date fault` MEANS `fact — a computer or chip's handling of a date change, including year 2000 or a leap year, contributed`
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk H` (LIST `a date fault`, `fact — a flood`) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS LIST `VIII.2 Part 1 — a date change contributed`
#ASSERT `the reasons` (`a building claim` `risk H` (LIST `a date fault`, `fact — a storm or tempest`) EMPTY EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `X12 — the short-period scale claims three months twice`

-- Ending exactly 3 months after the start: "Đến 3 tháng" (30%) and "Từ 3 đến 6 tháng"
-- (60%) both describe it. The encoding gives the lower row (fork F24).
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the short-period rate` `the Summary` (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS 30%

§§ `X13 — the refund on Bao Minh's cancellation counts seven days twice`

-- Notice on 2 July; cover to 9 July; refund counted from 2 July: 6,000,000, the premium
-- for 182 of 364 days, though the policy ran 189.
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the day Bao Minh's cancellation takes effect` (YMD 2026 7 2) EQUALS YMD 2026 7 9
#ASSERT `VI.4 — the premium Bao Minh refunds when it cancels` `the Summary` (YMD 2026 7 2) EQUALS 6000000

§§ `X14 — any condition, whatever its connection with the loss, defeats the claim`

-- A storm blows the roof off. The Insured had not kept the gutters in good repair
-- (VI.6), which had nothing to do with the roof. Nothing is payable.
`a storm, gutters neglected` MEANS
    `a claim in full` `the Summary` `risk G` `the day` (`the facts` (LIST `fact — a storm or tempest`))
        (LIST (`at the insured location` "Hanoi" (LIST (`physical damage to` `the building` `of` 200000000 `with` EMPTY))))
        `the premium paid on 10 January 2026` EMPTY EMPTY EMPTY
        (`conduct` (YMD 2026 6 11) (LIST `lapse — not: kept the insured property in good repair and took every proper measure to prevent DAMAGE`)) FALSE 0
#ASSERT `the amount payable` `a storm, gutters neglected` EQUALS 0

§§ `X17 — a short payment term lengthens the time to pay`

-- With an agreed premium payment term of 15 days, VIII.3.1(c) allows payment until the
-- end of the period; with none, the deadline is 30 days from acceptance.
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1 — the last day to pay the premium, or its first instalment` (`The premium` WITH `date cover was accepted` IS YMD 2026 1 1, `Bao Minh accepted payment in instalments` IS FALSE, `date the premium was paid in full` IS NOTHING, `instalments` IS EMPTY, `an agreed premium payment term, in days` IS JUST 15) `the Summary` EQUALS YMD 2026 12 31
#ASSERT `VIII.3.1 — the last day to pay the premium, or its first instalment` (`a premium paid on` NOTHING) `the Summary` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 31
